"""Original Section A practice questions and mock-paper content."""
BANK = [
('Strings','What does "REVISION".substring(2, 5) return?','VIS. The end index 5 is excluded.'),
('Strings','Evaluate "PLANE".compareTo("PLANT").','-15: first unequal characters E and T differ by 69 - 84.'),
('Strings','String s = "Blue"; s.toUpperCase(); System.out.println(s); Give the output.','Blue. The returned String was not assigned; the original String is immutable.'),
('Strings','Evaluate "CABANA".indexOf(\'A\') + "CABANA".lastIndexOf(\'A\').','6, because the indices are 1 and 5.'),
('Operators and conversions','int x = 4; int y = x++ + ++x; State x and y.','x = 6, y = 10. The left operand contributes 4, then the right contributes 6.'),
('Operators and conversions','Evaluate 17 / 4 + 17 % 4 in Java.','5. Integer quotient 4 plus remainder 1.'),
('Operators and conversions','Give the output: System.out.println(\'D\' + 2 + " " + (char)(\'D\' + 2));','70 F. char arithmetic promotes to int unless explicitly converted back.'),
('Operators and conversions','Give the values of "x" + 2 + 3 and 2 + 3 + "x".','x23 and 5x respectively; + is evaluated left to right.'),
('Math methods','Evaluate Math.floor(-2.3) + Math.ceil(2.3).','0.0, from -3.0 + 3.0.'),
('Math methods','Evaluate Math.pow(8, 2 / 3).','1.0. Integer division makes the exponent 0.'),
('Math methods','Evaluate Math.sqrt(Math.abs(-81)).','9.0.'),
('Math methods','Write Java for sqrt(p squared + q squared) divided by (p + q). Assume double p, q and a non-zero denominator.','Math.sqrt(p * p + q * q) / (p + q)'),
('Loops and control flow','Trace: for(int i = 1; i <= 5; i += 2) System.out.print(i + " "); State the number of body executions.','1 3 5; three executions.'),
('Loops and control flow','int i; for(i = 3; i < 1; i++) System.out.print(i); System.out.println(i * 2); Give output and body count.','6; the loop body executes zero times.'),
('Loops and control flow','int x = 2; do { x -= 3; } while(x > 0); State x and the body count.','x = -1; one execution, because do-while tests after the body.'),
('Loops and control flow','How many times does count++ run? for(int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) for(int j = 1; j <= i; j++) count++;','6 = 1 + 2 + 3.'),
('Arrays and algorithms','int[][] m = {{2,5,8},{1,4,7}}; State the order and m[1][2].','Order 2 by 3; value 7.'),
('Arrays and algorithms','How many bytes do the element values of int[4][3] require? Ignore object/header overhead.','4 * 3 * 4 = 48 bytes.'),
('Arrays and algorithms','Give the correct way to obtain the number of elements in array a and the number of characters in String s.','a.length and s.length() respectively.'),
('Arrays and algorithms','What ordering condition is needed for ordinary ascending binary search? How are bounds updated?','The array must be sorted ascending. If key < a[mid], high = mid - 1; if key > a[mid], low = mid + 1.'),
('Methods','Can void test(int n) and int test(int n) overload each other? Explain.','No. Return type alone cannot distinguish overloads; their parameter lists are identical.'),
('Methods','Write a method prototype check that accepts an int and returns boolean.','boolean check(int n)'),
('Methods','If int v = 7 is passed to void change(int p) { p = 99; }, what is v after the call?','7. The method receives a copy of the primitive argument value.'),
('Methods','Can a static method directly access a non-static field without an object reference?','No. It must use an instance, for example obj.count.'),
('Constructors','Distinguish a compiler-provided default constructor from an explicitly written no-argument constructor.','A default constructor is supplied when no constructor is declared. A programmer can instead declare a no-argument constructor explicitly.'),
('Constructors','class Box { int n; Box(int v) { n = v; } } What is n in new Box(9)?','9.'),
('Constructors','State two rules about a constructor name and return type.','Its name matches the class exactly; it has no return type, including no void.'),
('Constructors','What is constructor overloading? Give example signatures for class Box.','Several constructors with different parameter lists, for example Box() and Box(int n).'),
('Library classes','Evaluate Double.parseDouble("14.5") + Integer.parseInt("5").','19.5.'),
('Library classes','State the type and value returned by Character.isDigit(\'8\').','boolean, true.'),
('Library classes','State the type and value returned by Character.toUpperCase(\'q\').','char, Q.'),
('Library classes','Identify the conversions: Integer obj = 12; int n = obj;','The first uses autoboxing; the second uses unboxing.'),
('Classes, packages and access','Describe a class and an object using state and behaviour.','A class specifies fields and methods; an object is an instance with its own state and access to the defined behaviour.'),
('Classes, packages and access','What is encapsulation? Give a simple Java technique that supports it.','Bundling state and operations in a class and controlling access; for example private fields accessed through methods.'),
('Classes, packages and access','Name the package of Scanner and the package of Character and Integer.','Scanner: java.util. Character and Integer: java.lang.'),
('Classes, packages and access','State the access scope of private and public class members.','private: within the declaring class. public: available from other code wherever the declaring type is accessible.'),
('Correction and rewriting','Correct the array traversal boundary: for(int i = 0; i <= a.length; i++) System.out.println(a[i]);','Use i < a.length. The final valid index is a.length - 1.'),
('Correction and rewriting','A factorial program sets int f = 0 and repeatedly performs f *= i. Identify and fix the problem.','Logical error: initialize f to 1 before the loop.'),
('Correction and rewriting','boolean equal = a.compareTo(b); is intended to test equal String contents. Correct it.','boolean equal = a.equals(b); compareTo returns int, whereas equals returns boolean.'),
('Correction and rewriting','Use a ternary expression to assign "Eligible" when age >= 16 and "Not eligible" otherwise.','String result = age >= 16 ? "Eligible" : "Not eligible";'),
]

MCQ = [
('In Robot r = new Robot(); which identifies the class and the object reference?',
 ['r is the class; Robot is the reference','Robot is the class; r is the reference','Both are class names','Both are primitive values'],'B','Robot is the type; r refers to the created object.'),
('How many bytes are needed for the element values of a char[3][4] array, excluding overhead?', ['12','48','96','24'],'D','12 char values at 2 bytes each.'),
('What is "STUDY".substring(1,4)?',['TUD','TUDY','STU','UDY'],'A','Indices 1, 2 and 3 are selected.'),
('What does Math.pow(9, 1/2) return?',['3.0','0.0','1.0','4.5'],'C','1/2 is integer division, so the exponent is zero.'),
('What is Character.isLetterOrDigit(\'#\')?',['true','false','\'#\'','A char value'],'B','The character is neither a letter nor a digit.'),
('Which pair cannot be overloaded in the same class?', ['void f(int x) and void f(double x)','int f(int x) and int f(int x,int y)','void f(int x) and int f(int x)','void f(String s) and void f(char c)'],'C','Only the return type differs.'),
('Which member access modifier is the most restrictive?', ['private','public','protected','static'],'A','private limits access to the declaring class.'),
('The parameter of Integer.parseInt used in this syllabus is of which type?', ['int','double','char','String'],'D','It parses a String representing an integer.'),
('int x = 5; x += x++; What is the final value of x?', ['6','10','11','12'],'B','The saved left value 5 is added to the postfix expression value 5.'),
('What is Math.floor(-3.2)?', ['-3.0','3.0','-4.0','4.0'],'C','Floor moves towards negative infinity.'),
('What is "BANANA".lastIndexOf(\'A\')?', ['5','6','1','3'],'A','The final A is at index 5.'),
('Which is the final valid index of a non-empty array a?', ['a.length()','a.length','a.length()-1','a.length-1'],'D','Array length is a field; indices start at zero.'),
('Assertion: s.toUpperCase() does not modify the existing String object. Reason: String objects are immutable.',
 ['Both true; the reason explains the assertion','Both true; the reason does not explain the assertion','Assertion true; reason false','Assertion false; reason true'],'A','The method returns a String result rather than mutating the existing object.'),
('Ordinary binary search requires the input array to be:', ['All positive','Sorted in the order assumed by the algorithm','All distinct','Of even length'],'B','The ordering allows a half of the search interval to be discarded.'),
('After one complete left-to-right ascending bubble-sort pass on 7, 2, 5, 1, the array is:', ['1,2,5,7','2,1,5,7','2,5,1,7','7,5,2,1'],'C','Adjacent swaps move 7 to the end.'),
('int n; for(n = 3; n > 0; n--); System.out.println(n); What is printed?', ['3','2','1','0'],'D','The semicolon is the empty loop body. Printing occurs afterwards.'),
('When does the compiler supply a default constructor for a class?', ['When no constructor is declared','Whenever main exists','Whenever fields are private','For every declared constructor'],'A','Declaring any constructor prevents automatic provision of a default constructor.'),
('What is the return type of String.equals(String)?',['int','boolean','char','String'],'B','The result indicates content equality.'),
('A nested loop has three outer iterations and four inner iterations for each. How many inner-body executions occur?', ['7','3','4','12'],'D','3 multiplied by 4.'),
('Which Scanner method reads a complete line including spaces?', ['next()','nextChar()','nextLine()','readString()'],'C','nextLine reads the remainder of a line.'),
]

